## Checklist

- [x] I have searched for related issues but did not get the expected help.
- [x] This bug has not been fixed in the latest version.
- [x] The reproduction below is minimal, self-contained, and includes the observed result.

## 🐞 Detailed Description of the Problem

**Current:** with the UI language set to Simplified Chinese, cancelling a queued run answers in English. The action itself is translated — the Runs panel says `排队中的运行` / `取消排队中的运行` — but the toast the app pushes with its result is a hardcoded English sentence, and the same is true for the three other outcomes:

- cancel succeeded → **`Queued run cancelled`**
- the run already started → title **`Run already started`**, detail **`The queued run has already started; use Stop to cancel the active run.`** (which also names the English button `Stop`)
- the run already finished → **`Run already finished`**
- any other status → title **`Queued run updated`**, detail **`Current status: <status>`**

**Expected:** the toast is translated like every other outcome the user hears about (the neighbouring `error.cancelQueuedRun` key exists in both locales), so a Chinese user reads the result of the button they pressed in Chinese.

### Where

`apps/web/src/run-stream/model.ts:130-142` (read on `main` `89cd2d30c93e11c6e98e264cc08b171f6a3705f0`, blob `74c972ea11ad`):

```ts
export function queuedCancelToast(status: SessionRun["status"]): { detail?: string; title: string; tone: "error" | "info" } {
  if (status === "cancelled") return { title: "Queued run cancelled", tone: "info" };
  if (isActiveRunStatus(status)) {
    return {
      detail: "The queued run has already started; use Stop to cancel the active run.",
      title: "Run already started",
      tone: "info",
    };
  }
  if (isTerminalRunStatus(status)) return { title: "Run already finished", tone: "info" };
  return { detail: `Current status: ${status}`, title: "Queued run updated", tone: "info" };
}
```

Nothing in the function can reach a translator, and the toast is pushed verbatim at `apps/web/src/App.tsx:3802-3803`:

```ts
const toast = queuedCancelToast(cancelled.status);
pushToast(toast.tone, toast.title, toast.detail);
```

`apps/web/src/i18n/messages.ts` carries the *action* keys (`app.queuedRuns`, `app.queued`, `app.cancelQueuedRun`) and the *failure* key (`error.cancelQueuedRun`) in both locales, but no key for any of these four outcomes — so there is nothing for the effect to reuse.

The reason this is not the closed localization sweep is visible in history: `4f3b802f fix(web): localize run failure guidance and collapse diagnostics` (2026-10-25) is the last commit that touched this file and localized the failure guidance next to these lines, and the English text is *pinned by a test* — `apps/web/tests/ComposerRunAction.test.tsx:195-201` asserts `{ title: "Queued run cancelled" }`, `"Run already started"`, `"Run already finished"`. Any sweep that only greps the source would have seen that test as proof the strings were intended.

### Red-first reproduction (fails on `main` `89cd2d30`)

```ts
// apps/web/tests/queuedCancelToast.test.ts
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { queuedCancelToast } from "../src/run-stream/model.js";
import { zhCN } from "../src/i18n/messages.js";

const asked: string[] = [];
const t = (key: string) => { asked.push(key); return "翻译后的文案"; };

queuedCancelToast("cancelled", t);           // the fixed signature passes the translator in
assert.ok(asked.length > 0, "the cancel outcome must go through the message catalog");
assert.ok(Object.keys(zhCN).some((key) => key.startsWith("app.queuedCancelOutcome")));
```

Observed on `main` `89cd2d30` with `cd apps/web && node --import tsx --test tests/queuedCancelToast.test.ts`:

```
# CANCELLED_TOAST {"title":"Queued run cancelled","tone":"info"}
# TRANSLATOR_CALLS 0
# AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: the cancel outcome must go through the message catalog
# pass 0 # fail 1
```

**Suggested fix (one PR):** give `queuedCancelToast` the translator (`(status, t)`) and return `t(...)` for the four titles and two details, add the keys to `en` and `zhCN`, and update the three assertions in `apps/web/tests/ComposerRunAction.test.tsx` to compare message keys rather than English literals so the next sweep cannot re-pin them. Six strings, one pure function, no data dependency.

## Environment

- `main` `89cd2d30c93e11c6e98e264cc08b171f6a3705f0`
- `node v22.23.2`, `pnpm 11.1.2`, Linux x64
- UI language set to `中文 (简体)`; Runs panel → a queued run → `取消排队中的运行`
- Reproduce: `cd apps/web && node --import tsx --test tests/queuedCancelToast.test.ts`

## Version Information

- ScienceDiscovery `main` @ `89cd2d30c93e11c6e98e264cc08b171f6a3705f0` (2026-11-04)
- Affected surface: composer Runs panel → cancel a queued run (toast), both web and desktop shells

