Those helpers throw a plain `Error`, not an `ApiStatusError` and not a `SessionStoreHttpError`:

- `services/api/src/artifacts/index.ts:169` — `if (!version) throw new Error("Artifact version not found");` (blob `2d9539265751`)
- `services/api/src/artifacts/index.ts:349` — `if (!to) throw new Error("Artifact version not found");` (the `?against=` id on the diff route)

Nothing downstream recognises that message, so the top-level catch falls through to its last branch: `isKnownClientInputError` (`services/api/src/http/error-classification.ts:20`, blob `38b0b962dac9`) only matches `is required` / `must` / `unknown value` / `cannot` / `does not match` / `invalid` / `unsafe … path|archive|package` / `plain basename`, and the 404 message regex in `http/index.ts:3924` only covers `Project|Session|Proxy server|Provider|Model not found` and `Execution|Transfer|Timer|Subagent not found: …`. `Artifact version not found` matches neither → 500 `Internal server error` + `apiLog.error("unclassified_request_error", …)`.

User impact: a stale artifact link, a version deleted by retention, or a diff against a version that no longer exists is reported as a server failure. The Artifact modal reads content and provenance together (`apps/web/src/ScientificArtifacts.tsx:686`), so this is also the status a reader sees when the version is simply gone.

